        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 12,
        "headingId": 435,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-11-11T10:50:07"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 479,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 436,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 66406,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 12,
        "headingId": 436,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-11-11T10:50:07"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 480,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 437,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 66407,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 12,
        "headingId": 437,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Tumours are typically solitary and peripheral. Rare hilar tumours have been reported {3759064; 10029443; 18184418}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-11-11T10:50:07"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 481,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 438,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 66408,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 12,
        "headingId": 438,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Tumours are usually incidental findings in asymptomatic patients. Radiologically, the tumours are well circumscribed, homogeneous, and non-calcified. Cystic spaces may be seen on CT or MRI, and low-level PET positivity has been reported {10029443; 11956369; 22214375}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-11-11T10:50:07"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 482,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 439,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 66409,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 12,
        "headingId": 439,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Alveolar adenoma is very rare, has a slight female predominance, and has a reported age range of 39&ndash;74&nbsp;years {3759064; 10029443; 18184418}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-11-11T10:50:07"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 483,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 440,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 66410,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 12,
        "headingId": 440,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The etiology of alveolar adenoma is controversial. Chromosomal aberrations support a neoplastic origin, but it is unclear whether both epithelial and mesenchymal components are neoplastic {15173924}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-11-11T10:50:07"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 484,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 441,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 66411,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 12,
        "headingId": 441,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Alveolar adenoma appears to represent a combined proliferation of alveolar pneumocytes and septal mesenchyme, but the pathogenesis is unknown. No characteristic molecular profile has been identified. Microsatellite abnormalities have been demonstrated in the epithelial component but not the mesenchymal component {15173924}. Diploid DNA pattern has been reported {18184418}. A non-balanced translocation t(10;16) has been reported in some cases {8689607}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-11-11T10:50:07"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 491,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 448,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 66412,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 12,
        "headingId": 448,
        "headingText": "<p>Tumours measure 7&ndash;60 mm and are well demarcated, with smooth, lobulated, multicystic pale-yellow to tan cut surfaces {3759064; 10029443; 18184418}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2021-02-02T10:38:12"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 485,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 442,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 66413,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 12,
        "headingId": 442,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Alveolar adenomas are well circumscribed; composed of multiple cystic spaces frequently resembling alveolar spaces that are filled with eosinophilic granular material; and lined by cytologically bland, flattened to cuboidal epithelial cells, which correspond to type&nbsp;II pneumocytes by immunohistochemical and electron microscopic evaluation {10029443; 8917711}. Associated stroma may be myxoid or collagenous, containing cytologically bland spindle cells {10029443; 3759064}.</p>\r\n<p>Cyst lining cells are positive for cytokeratin, TTF1, napsin&nbsp;A, and surfactant protein. Stromal cells are negative for these markers and may show focal staining for SMA and MSA and rare staining for S100 and CD34 {10029443; 23118769}. Cytokeratin and TTF1 staining of the pneumocytes differentiates alveolar adenoma from lymphangioma, where the endothelial cells are keratin-negative. Lack of staining for TTF1 in stromal cells, along with the absence of a spectrum of solid papillary, sclerotic, and haemorrhagic patterns, helps differentiate alveolar adenoma from sclerosing pneumocytoma, which typically lacks cystic structures and shows TTF1-positive stromal cells.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-11-11T10:50:07"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 486,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 443,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 66414,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 12,
        "headingId": 443,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Cytological features of alveolar adenoma are poorly described.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-11-11T10:50:07"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 487,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 444,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 66415,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 12,
        "headingId": 444,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-11-11T10:50:07"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 490,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 447,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 66416,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 12,
        "headingId": 447,
        "headingText": "<p><em>Essential:</em></p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Well-circumscribed tumour composed of cystic spaces frequently resembling alveolar spaces, lined by a single layer of type&nbsp;II pneumocytes overlying a mesenchymal, sometimes myxoid, stroma of variable thickness</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p><em>Desirable:</em></p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>The pneumocytes are characteristically positive for TTF1</li>\r\n</ul>",
        "timestamp": "2020-12-18T17:46:30"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 488,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 445,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 66417,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 12,
        "headingId": 445,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-11-11T10:50:07"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 489,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 446,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 66418,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 12,
        "headingId": 446,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Alveolar adenomas are benign and surgical excision is curative {10029443}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2020-11-11T10:50:07"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
]